<article class="env-lemma" id="012V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/012V">Lemma <span data-tag="012V">12.24.10</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $(K^\bullet , F)$ be a filtered complex of $\mathcal{A}$. The associated spectral sequence </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
weakly converges to $H^*(K^\bullet )$ if and only if for every $p, q \in \mathbf{Z}$ we have equality in equations (<a href="/tag/012T" data-tag="012T">12.24.6.2</a>) and (<a href="/tag/012S" data-tag="012S">12.24.6.1</a>), 
</p>
</li><li><p>
abuts to $H^*(K)$ if and only if it weakly converges to $H^*(K^\bullet )$ and we have $\bigcap _ p (\mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(d) \cap F^ pK^ n + \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(d) \cap K^ n) = \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(d) \cap K^ n$ and $\bigcup _ p (\mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(d) \cap F^ pK^ n + \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(d) \cap K^ n) = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(d) \cap K^ n$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from the discussions above. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
